## Summary
Iceland is set to hold a referendum on restarting negotiations to join the European Union. Opinion polls indicate that public opinion is evenly split on the issue, with a deadlocked vote expected.

## Key Points
- Iceland will conduct a referendum on restarting EU membership negotiations.
- The referendum focuses on whether to resume talks for EU accession.
- Public sentiment is divided, with polls showing a balance between supporters and opponents.


